hile* staying attuned to your son.** - **If he's struggling:** > \" I see this is hard. Let's try one together, then you do the next one alone. I'll be right here if you get stuck.\" - **If he's confident:** > \" I trust you can do this. I'll check your work when you're done — no help, just feedback.\" - **If the teacher * truly* means no help:** > \" I'll step back completely, but I'll * still* praise his effort: ' I'm proud you're trying on your own!' \" ### 🌟 **Why this isn't about \" right or wrong\":** - ** parenting isn't about following rules perfectly** — it's about * adaptability*. - ** the \" sacred\" here is your son's * actual* experience** — not a rigid \" no help\" rule. - ** your role is to * observe* and * adjust*,** not to \" be right.\" > \"The best teachers and parents don't ask ' * am I doing this right?*' — they ask ' * is this helping him grow?'* and * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *